1
00:00:00,710 --> 00:00:03,130
(Sheldon:)73 is the 21st prime number.

2
00:00:03,130 --> 00:00:07,120
(Sheldon:)Its mirror, 37, is the 12th,
and its mirror, 21,

3
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:08,820
(Sheldon:)is the product of multiplying--

4
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:12,190
(Sheldon:)hang on to your hats--
seven and three.

5
00:00:12,860 --> 00:00:16,190
(Sheldon:)Eh? Eh? Did I lie?

6
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:17,230
(Leonard:)We get it.

7
00:00:17,230 --> 00:00:20,100
(Leonard:)73 is the Chuck Norris
of numbers.

8
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,800
(Sheldon:)Chuck Norris wishes.

9
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:25,220
In binary 73 is a palindrome:

10
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:28,210
"one-zero-zero-
one-zero-zero-one"

11
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:31,680
which backwards is "one-zero-
zero-one-zero-zero-one"--

12
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:33,050
(Sheldon:)exactly the same.

13
00:00:33,050 --> 00:00:37,450
(Sheldon:)All Chuck Norris backwards
gets you is: "Sirron Kcuhc."

14
00:00:37,450 --> 00:00:39,480
(Raj:)Just for the record,

15
00:00:39,490 --> 00:00:43,040
when you enter 5,318,008
on a calculator,

16
00:00:43,040 --> 00:00:45,960
upside-down it spells "boobies""

17
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,330
(Leonard:)Remember when you were wondering

18
00:00:50,330 --> 00:00:52,500
(Leonard:)why the girls didn't
want to eat with us tonight?

19
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,500
(Howard:)Yeah, I get it now.

20
00:00:55,640 --> 00:00:58,140
(Penny:)I love your little
heart locket, Bernadette.

21
00:00:58,140 --> 00:00:59,470
(Bernadette:)Oh, thanks.

22
00:00:59,470 --> 00:01:00,770
(Bernadette:)Howard gave it to me.

